Apps, services, machines, and employees are part of the attack surface. You said they’re “attack areas, but not necessarily surface areas.” In fact, they’re the main part of it. The attack surface isn’t only physical. It covers everything an attacker could target:

Digital: open ports, web apps, cloud services, APIs, every device on the network
Physical: server rooms, USB ports, spare network sockets in the office
Human: every employee who could be phished, vished, or impersonated

